# cargo-mutants writes per-mutant log files (one cargo test transcript
# per mutant) under mutants.out/log/. These are useful for debugging a
# specific mutant locally but should not be committed:
# - they are very large (29MB+ per crate)
# - they have absolute paths in them (workspace-rooted)
# - the structured outcome is captured in caught.txt / missed.txt /
#   timeout.txt / unviable.txt and the per-crate <date>.json summary,
#   which IS committed.
**/mutants.out/log/

# debug.log carries the same per-mutant detail and the cargo-mutants
# version-specific timing trace. Not committed.
**/mutants.out/debug.log
